<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malawi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Republic of Malawi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malawi is a landlocked country in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, lying along the western shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malawi">Lake Malawi</a>. Its name recalls the Maravi confederacy of the 16th and 17th centuries. It became a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1891, renamed Nyasaland in 1907, was joined to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federation-of-rhodesia-and-nyasaland">Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland</a> in 1953, and became independent under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hastings-banda">Hastings Banda</a> in 1964.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malawi.jpg" alt="Malawi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: Achim1999 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Malawi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
